I don't know about this, because whenever I tried to read an older bones file
from a newer version, NetHack just crashed.  But the level you describe
pops up every once in a while.  It is a Rogue-type level.  (The original Rogue
looked VERY much like this level.  There are a maximum of 9 rooms per level,
arranged in a tic-tac-toe-style pattern, there are no doors, any special
graphics [if you're on a micro] are replaced with the old text characters,
etc.)  It was thrown in, I assume, as humor, and I did enjoy it.

The only thing I dislike about the Rogue level is that almost all the rooms
are dark, causing me to use many charges from a wand of light, or whatever.
